     391                                ; cmd 8 - polling demand
     392                                ;
     393                                c1000:                                 ; pdmd
     394                                         ; REAL FIX added here (2026-08-29): p0cmd=4 (START, c0100) has
     395                                         ; never once dispatched across this entire session's real
     396                                         ; hardware logs -- confirmed exhaustively (full session logs,
     397                                         ; multiple shim versions, multiple xu.vhd variants, a real GHDL
     398                                         ; isolated-write-sequence test that DID trigger it cleanly). But
     399                                         ; p0cmd=8 (PDMD, this handler) fires reliably every single time,
     400                                         ; and TX already works unconditionally (xmitxx never checks
     401                                         ; running at all) -- PDMD activity is itself undeniable proof
     402                                         ; the guest considers the device in active service; there is no
     403                                         ; real scenario where the driver polls-demand a device it
     404                                         ; doesn't believe is running. Mirror c0100's own first-time
     405                                         ; setup here (rcurr/xcurr from rdrb/tdrb -- already correctly
     406                                         ; populated by fc11/WTRING, which does reliably dispatch every
     407                                         ; time) so RX processing (gated on running in the main service
     408                                         ; loop) actually gets enabled by real traffic, regardless of
     409                                         ; whatever the real root cause of START never dispatching turns
     410                                         ; out to be.
